CRIMINAL PROCEDURE CODE (CHAPTER 7) NOTIFICATION MADE UNDER SECTION ll(1)

S 2711989 2001 Edition

REVISED EDITION 2021 B. L. R.O. 10/2021

LAWS OF BRUNEI Criminal Procedure Code CAP.7,N 1 3 [Subsidiary]

SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION Notification made under section ll(1) conferring special jurisdiction on Magistrates The Chief Justice has conferred upon the following Magistrates, with effect fiom 1st February 1989, special jurisdiction in a Court presided over by any such Magistrate by increasing the power to pass a sentence of imprisonment to a term of 7 years and a fine of $10,000 -

(a) the person occupying the post of Chief Magistrate;

(b) the person occupying the post of Senior Magistrate;

(c) the person occupying the post of Chief Registrar;

(d) the person occupying the post of Deputy Chief Registrar;

(e) any person occupying the post of Registrar; and @ any qualified person meaning a person who is qualified for the purposes of the Legal Profession Act (Chapter 132) by virtue of section 3 thereof, occupying the post of Magistrate. B.L.R.O. 10/2021
